# BeefNet (domain)

## Non-negotiables

- Prefix `COB`; channel **`GUILD`** always (default is PARTY)
- Never apply `RANK_COMMIT` without verifying sender Officer+ via roster `rankIndex`
- If roster not loaded: queue or drop — **never** apply unverified
- Net validates shape then calls Core — Net does not invent ranks
- Custom `CHANNEL` addon chat is **forbidden** on Classic

## Wire defaults

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Prefix | `COB` (≤16 chars; register once) |
| Channel | `GUILD` — pass explicitly |
| Body | ≤ **255** chars; colon-delimited / small packed strings |
| Pacing | ChatThrottleLib-class (or AceComm wrapping CTL) |

Do not use `RAID`/`PARTY` for ladder state.

## Message types (V1)

| Type | Who emits | Receiver duty |
|------|-----------|---------------|
| `HELLO` | Anyone | Soft version warn; no ladder mutate |
| `RANK_COMMIT` | Officer+ only | Roster rank-index gate, then Core apply |
| `SUGGESTION` | Member | Officers filter; never auto-promote |
| `SCORE_EVENT` | Prefer local | Off-wire by default; never high-frequency |
| `SYNC_REQUEST` | Login/reload | Once per settle + backoff |
| `SYNC_STATE` | Prefer one peer (officer first) | Chunk + suppress duplicates |

## Trust & sync

- `CHAT_MSG_ADDON` sender names are server-supplied — trustworthy identity
- Major protocol mismatch → soft warn; discard incompatible commits
- Sync on login settle (`COB.Sync:OnLogin`), not at `ADDON_LOADED` / file scope

## Anti-spam

- ~10 msgs/prefix regenerating ~1/s — CTL must prevent `AddonMessageThrottle`
- Login sync: random reply delay + suppress if another peer already answered `reqId`
- Prefer revision diffs / chunks over dumping the whole guild in one frame
- Guild spectacle: **one** throttled line from the approving officer’s client only
- Do not broadcast every score tick — official path is officer Commit (+ sync types)
